WEBVTT

00:03.218 --> 00:07.718
In Egypt, an old hag named Enyaba
once told me:

00:08.223 --> 00:11.100
Fire at whomever
the arrow desires.

00:11.559 --> 00:14.270
For the impaled
shall become your ally.

00:14.479 --> 00:16.272
The speared shall witness,

00:16.314 --> 00:20.609
rising from the deep recesses
of their soul, a single unique power.

00:23.113 --> 00:26.116
Stands is what
I think she called them.

00:26.783 --> 00:28.951
Jotaro Kujo and his minions…

00:29.744 --> 00:34.244
If there are more hit men
in Morioh in pursuit of my dear Yoshikage,

00:35.917 --> 00:39.295
then my Stand users,
my allies, shall multiply by my hand.

00:39.671 --> 00:42.965
So, arrow! Whom do you desire?

00:43.007 --> 00:45.801
Select your prey! Go forth!

00:45.969 --> 00:47.971
PULL

00:49.264 --> 00:50.265
A telephone pole?

00:50.306 --> 00:52.308
What does
a telephone pole have t—?

00:53.393 --> 00:57.105
You… You desire that child?

00:58.273 --> 01:02.485
You're trying to tell me
that child will become my ally?

01:04.279 --> 01:06.281
Then so be it.

01:06.322 --> 01:09.491
All I have to do is pierce
the lad's soul, right?

01:29.053 --> 01:29.803
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

01:29.804 --> 01:31.931
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

01:31.973 --> 01:34.308
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

01:34.350 --> 01:37.603
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

01:38.354 --> 01:40.481
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

01:40.523 --> 01:42.858
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

01:42.942 --> 01:46.195
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

01:46.404 --> 01:49.907
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

01:50.700 --> 01:54.120
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

01:54.162 --> 01:56.789
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

01:56.831 --> 01:58.999
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

01:59.042 --> 02:01.044
<i>I will chase you</i>

02:01.127 --> 02:02.753
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

02:02.837 --> 02:05.381
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

02:05.465 --> 02:07.508
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

02:07.550 --> 02:10.261
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

02:10.470 --> 02:14.970
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

02:16.184 --> 02:20.684
<i>So I chase you</i>

02:24.108 --> 02:27.903
EPISODE 26
ROSHAM BOY IS HERE!

02:39.290 --> 02:42.293
So it's Rohan Kishibe,
manga artist extraordinaire.

02:42.377 --> 02:44.420
Good morning, Mr. Joestar.

02:44.754 --> 02:47.757
Snapping a few photos I see…

02:47.840 --> 02:50.342
I'm trying to capture candid shots
of office workers

02:50.385 --> 02:51.969
in their morning commute.

02:53.054 --> 02:55.473
If Yoshikage Kira really did steal
someone's identity at

02:55.556 --> 02:57.766
Beauty Institute Cinderella,

02:58.059 --> 03:00.102
we can safely assume
he's commuting every morning,

03:00.144 --> 03:01.770
just like his victim once did.

03:01.938 --> 03:03.397
Commuting…

03:03.982 --> 03:07.235
Knowing he's a man between
the ages of 25 and 35

03:07.277 --> 03:10.113
around 175 centimeters
tall and an office worker

03:10.154 --> 03:11.780
helps narrow the suspect pool.

03:11.823 --> 03:13.115
I see…

03:13.157 --> 03:16.285
But how do you know
he uses this station…

03:16.577 --> 03:18.996
He could just
as easily commute by car.

03:19.080 --> 03:20.498
That is a possibility.

03:20.748 --> 03:23.167
He may have changed his face,

03:23.334 --> 03:26.378
but, in many ways,
he's likely still very much himself.

03:26.713 --> 03:30.216
You can be sure the family of
one of these men is already

03:30.258 --> 03:32.635
wary of bizarre behavior.

03:35.179 --> 03:38.015
My fear is that the family
will recognize their intruder,

03:38.057 --> 03:40.934
which would likely prompt
him to eliminate them as well.

03:41.269 --> 03:43.813
I'm not getting soft, mind you…

03:44.105 --> 03:47.024
We must simply locate Kira
before he can wreak more havoc.

03:48.401 --> 03:50.027
Hey!

03:53.323 --> 03:56.159
Mister, wanna play roshambo?

03:56.284 --> 03:58.452
Ro-sham…

03:58.536 --> 04:01.247
Come on. Can't ya play a little?

04:01.289 --> 04:02.707
Crazy kid…

04:02.915 --> 04:03.540
Ro-sham…

04:03.541 --> 04:07.086
I suppose every station
has its nut job…

04:07.587 --> 04:09.922
Well, if you happen to
come across any leads,

04:09.964 --> 04:11.924
you know how to reach me, Mr. Joestar.

04:11.966 --> 04:14.551
Don't go sticking your nose
in dangerous situations

04:14.635 --> 04:16.136
all by your lonesome now…

04:20.558 --> 04:23.477
Hey, Mister.
You're that manga drawer, right?

04:24.937 --> 04:27.147
You stopped drawing
for a while, right?

04:27.273 --> 04:30.150
I read <i>Shonen Jump</i> every week.

04:30.193 --> 04:33.529
So whaddya say… It wouldn't kill
ya to play with me.

04:34.322 --> 04:36.907
What's your problem? Beat it!

04:37.033 --> 04:41.533
I just wanna play roshambo.
Come on…

04:44.957 --> 04:49.457
What's with this little punk?
He's got a gaping hole in his cheek!

04:49.837 --> 04:51.547
- It's serious…
- Hey,

04:51.631 --> 04:53.257
- It must open up into his mouth…
- come on, come on!

04:53.424 --> 04:55.300
No hard feelings if you beat me.

04:55.593 --> 04:58.929
If it's a draw, we do it again.
If you're too late, you lose.

04:59.013 --> 05:00.889
Got it? Ready, and…

05:01.099 --> 05:02.225
Ro-sham…

05:02.266 --> 05:05.143
<i>This kid is being
weirdly tenacious.</i>

05:06.270 --> 05:08.063
<i>Is he a Stand user?</i>

05:11.192 --> 05:14.361
Okay… ro-sham…

05:14.862 --> 05:16.905
Heaven's Door!

05:24.831 --> 05:25.748
Hmph.

05:30.336 --> 05:31.503
Let's see…

05:31.629 --> 05:34.673
Name's Ken Oyanagi, age eleven.

05:35.383 --> 05:38.010
Nothing here about a Stand…

05:38.136 --> 05:40.763
The injury seems to be
from a fall from a telephone pole.

05:42.014 --> 05:46.018
"ROSHAMBO" FAN.
WILL PLAY "ROSHAMBO" AT ANY CHANCE.
PLAYS "SCISSORS" FIRST.

05:44.058 --> 05:46.039
So this kid plays roshambo
any chance he can get.

05:48.062 --> 05:49.021
Ridiculous, but…

05:49.063 --> 05:51.607
Hello sirs.
Will you be riding today or not?

05:51.732 --> 05:53.650
Could you please
give me 30 seconds?

05:56.737 --> 05:57.487
Fire away.

05:57.572 --> 05:59.782
Fine, let's go.
Then you'll leave me alone, right?

05:59.824 --> 06:01.992
Ro-sham… bo!

06:04.787 --> 06:06.205
Well, so long.

06:08.332 --> 06:10.625
I-I lost…

06:19.260 --> 06:21.512
I suppose that's enough work
for one day.

06:21.679 --> 06:23.555
Yo, Rohan-sensei.

06:23.598 --> 06:25.641
Calling it a day already, eh?

06:25.683 --> 06:28.268
Why don't you come and join us?

06:29.854 --> 06:32.439
<i>It's that jerk off Josuke,
and that moron Okuyasu…</i>

06:32.523 --> 06:34.608
<i>Not to mention bitchy Yukako.</i>

06:34.650 --> 06:37.402
<i>I have absolutely nothing
in common with any of them.</i>

06:37.612 --> 06:41.616
Sorry, but I'm actually working.
Some other time.

06:41.949 --> 06:43.158
I see…

06:45.953 --> 06:50.165
Hey, just what do you
think you're doing? That's my seat.

06:50.541 --> 06:53.043
You never sat down.

06:53.127 --> 06:57.131
The seat was up for grabs,
so I took it.

06:57.548 --> 06:58.799
Whoops.

06:58.841 --> 07:01.343
What's this all about?
Why won't you leave me alone?

07:01.427 --> 07:03.429
Let's settle this with
a little roshambo.

07:03.471 --> 07:04.930
Winner takes the seat.

07:04.972 --> 07:06.056
Again?!

07:09.977 --> 07:13.814
No! I sat here first!

07:13.856 --> 07:15.983
- This is my seat!
- Sir…

07:16.484 --> 07:17.526
Hang on…

07:17.735 --> 07:20.946
Rohan-sensei, give him a break.

07:20.988 --> 07:22.823
He's just a kid.

07:22.865 --> 07:26.034
Don't make the poor kid cry.
That's not very grown up of you.

07:26.077 --> 07:27.495
You could try sitting next to him…

07:27.537 --> 07:29.705
Shut up! Not another word,
all of you!

07:30.456 --> 07:32.958
Fine! I'll play you
roshambo again!

07:33.000 --> 07:35.043
That's what you want,
isn't it?

07:36.295 --> 07:40.795
Now that's more like it!
Get ready!

07:41.008 --> 07:44.011
Ro-sham… bo!

07:44.971 --> 07:48.224
Oh? Y-Yes, I win!

07:49.225 --> 07:50.851
Whatcha think of me now!

07:50.893 --> 07:54.938
I've never been so happy to
win roshambo in my life.

07:55.022 --> 07:57.190
- Not very grown up like…
- Not very grown up like…

07:58.025 --> 07:59.776
There's no better feeling…

07:59.860 --> 08:02.028
than destroying a little whelp
at his own game.

08:05.783 --> 08:08.160
D-Damn it!

08:16.419 --> 08:18.337
This is some good material…

08:18.379 --> 08:21.423
Who knew such an obscure book
could be found in Morioh?

08:21.674 --> 08:23.384
7,500 yen, huh…

08:23.759 --> 08:25.343
Do I have that much on me?

08:26.929 --> 08:29.973
Excuse me,
I wanna buy this book.

08:30.391 --> 08:32.059
You cursed…

08:33.853 --> 08:36.272
Shall we duke it out
roshambo style?

08:36.564 --> 08:37.898
Fine!

08:38.441 --> 08:41.485
Brace yourself! Ro-sham…

08:42.194 --> 08:43.778
Rock!

08:44.739 --> 08:47.074
You're messing
with the wrong artist!

08:48.826 --> 08:50.619
I won. See?

08:50.745 --> 08:52.455
I finally won!

08:54.582 --> 08:56.458
One win, two losses!

08:56.626 --> 08:58.794
What the hell is this?!

09:03.424 --> 09:04.174
Wh—

09:05.259 --> 09:06.343
What?!

09:06.719 --> 09:09.346
It can't be! His wound…

09:09.430 --> 09:11.807
Could he be a Stand user?!

09:12.725 --> 09:13.642
What?!

09:14.810 --> 09:16.812
S-So cool!

09:16.896 --> 09:19.356
Who knew he was hiding
something so cool!

09:19.482 --> 09:23.819
This energy flowing into me
is totally awesome!

09:23.861 --> 09:25.654
I'm feeling energized!

09:26.030 --> 09:27.990
H-Heaven's Door!

09:28.115 --> 09:30.283
Turn this brat into a book!

09:29.992 --> 09:30.742
OPEN

09:31.827 --> 09:33.245
CANNOT ATTACK ROHAN KISHIBE.

09:39.669 --> 09:41.128
This kid…

09:41.420 --> 09:44.464
seems that was the first time
he used his Stand.

09:45.174 --> 09:48.677
Could he be on his way to
becoming a Stand user?

09:50.304 --> 09:54.804
Hmph. "I want to beat the crap
out of Rohan in roshambo," huh?

09:55.059 --> 09:57.102
"Roshambo is not
a game of chance.

09:57.228 --> 09:59.521
It's a psychological
game of will.

09:59.563 --> 10:00.814
If I defeat Rohan at roshambo,

10:00.856 --> 10:03.608
then it means
I've outwitted the man himself.

10:03.776 --> 10:05.277
Rohan Kishibe is only 20 years old,

10:05.319 --> 10:07.612
but he lives life on his own,
and on his own terms.

10:07.780 --> 10:10.824
What's more, he inspires
countless people with his many works.

10:10.991 --> 10:13.827
If I can beat the crap out
of the revered Rohan in roshambo,

10:13.869 --> 10:16.872
I can one day be
even better than him.

10:16.997 --> 10:18.748
One day, I want to grow up

10:18.833 --> 10:21.001
and be revered and
respected like Rohan."

10:24.380 --> 10:25.839
There's no doubt about it,

10:25.881 --> 10:28.383
this kid is well on the road to
becoming a Stand user!

10:28.509 --> 10:30.636
The arrow must have only
just pierced his soul.

10:31.137 --> 10:35.637
"Ability… victory in roshambo means
my opponent's energy becomes my own.

10:35.808 --> 10:37.309
However, five games are necessary.

10:37.351 --> 10:40.187
Two wins means only
partial energy from my opponent."

10:40.312 --> 10:41.897
Five games?

10:41.856 --> 10:44.775
I CANNOT ATTACK ROHAN KISHIBE.

10:46.569 --> 10:49.488
I CAN ATTACK ROHAN KISHIBE.

10:49.864 --> 10:51.574
W-What?

10:51.615 --> 10:55.744
So awesome…
So this power's called a "Stand"?

10:55.786 --> 10:58.246
Thought you dodged
the bullet, eh…

10:58.330 --> 11:01.875
See, I already got
one-third of your Stand.

11:03.043 --> 11:05.545
My right arm is… gone!

11:05.588 --> 11:10.050
I've got one-third of Heaven's Door
under my control!

11:11.510 --> 11:15.180
No more mind-reading for you.

11:15.222 --> 11:16.556
Punk…

11:16.599 --> 11:21.099
If I win two more times,
all of your powers will be mine!

11:21.228 --> 11:25.106
You punk! Think you can
get away with this?!

11:27.735 --> 11:30.529
Pretty ballsy move,
punching me like that.

11:30.571 --> 11:32.948
It's called getting a taste
of your own medicine, ass!

11:33.240 --> 11:37.369
To get Heaven's Door's
right arm back,

11:37.411 --> 11:40.372
I'm going to have to win
at roshambo, eh…

11:42.082 --> 11:43.166
It's game on.

11:43.250 --> 11:45.210
Good!

11:44.043 --> 11:47.546
5 MATCHES
MATCH 1
MATCH 2
MATCH 3
MATCH 4
MATCH 5

11:49.340 --> 11:52.051
HEAVEN'S DOOR

11:52.593 --> 11:55.137
Are you oblivious
to your own plight?

11:55.221 --> 11:57.640
One more loss and
you're finished.

11:57.723 --> 12:00.392
You have to know
you're out of second chances.

12:00.434 --> 12:03.645
Now that I know you're a Stand user,
I shall have no mercy on you!

12:03.938 --> 12:05.814
The moment
I retrieve my right arm,

12:05.898 --> 12:07.524
I'm putting you
out of commission.

12:07.608 --> 12:08.692
And you know it.

12:08.776 --> 12:10.819
Are you trying to
psyche me out?

12:11.111 --> 12:13.279
All right, let's get
this little contest started.

12:13.447 --> 12:15.490
No, I'm not ready quite yet.

12:15.699 --> 12:18.159
I did just win with paper,

12:18.285 --> 12:21.746
and it's only natural to want to
go with rock or scissors next,

12:21.872 --> 12:24.916
then again that'd be
a real childish move.

12:24.959 --> 12:29.338
But you don't seem to
be the naive type, Rohan-sensei,

12:29.421 --> 12:33.842
so maybe going with paper
would be the best way to go.

12:34.343 --> 12:35.969
Right, I made up my mind.

12:36.595 --> 12:37.762
Here we go!

12:37.805 --> 12:40.808
Ro-sham… bo!

12:41.642 --> 12:42.643
What?!

12:42.685 --> 12:46.438
I did it!
I just outwitted Rohan with paper!

12:47.314 --> 12:49.774
ROHAN
KEN
5 MATCHES

12:47.481 --> 12:49.796
That makes two wins
and two losses.

12:49.984 --> 12:51.777
Now, then…

13:08.961 --> 13:11.380
I took your lower half.

13:11.463 --> 13:14.299
If you're tired, maybe we
should take a trip to the bench?

13:14.425 --> 13:16.885
No, that won't be necessary.

13:16.969 --> 13:20.263
The moment of victory
is best savored…

13:20.347 --> 13:23.308
while looking down on the conquered
with pity and disdain.

13:25.185 --> 13:27.061
I've got two wins
and two losses now,

13:27.313 --> 13:29.732
we're both one game away
from destiny.

13:29.773 --> 13:33.610
But now,
I can almost taste victory.

13:34.194 --> 13:37.697
I mean, after I lost twice,
I did win twice in a row.

13:37.781 --> 13:39.741
It's the other way around for you,
Rohan-sensei.

13:39.783 --> 13:41.242
You've lost twice in a row.

13:41.452 --> 13:44.580
You're smack dab in
the middle of a losing streak!

13:50.711 --> 13:51.920
Marvelous!

13:52.171 --> 13:54.756
I'd expect nothing less
from a kid chosen by the arrow!

13:54.798 --> 13:57.926
If this kid can take on
Rohan Kishibe's unique

13:58.010 --> 14:01.263
mind-reading powers,
we'll be invincible!

14:01.347 --> 14:04.308
You will serve my Yoshikage well.

14:05.100 --> 14:06.434
Hey punk…

14:06.477 --> 14:10.439
Your psychological ploys
have improved greatly.

14:10.481 --> 14:13.775
You've lost twice in a row,
that's a fact.

14:14.151 --> 14:16.611
Fact, huh… Indeed.

14:16.695 --> 14:20.782
In that case, allow me to
tell you another fact.

14:21.116 --> 14:24.577
For our next duel, paper will
most certainly not be your choice of attack.

14:27.247 --> 14:28.623
Guess we'll find out,
won't we…

14:28.707 --> 14:30.959
Hey, hey, hey, hey,
hey, hey, hold it.

14:31.085 --> 14:34.046
I used rock twice in
a row and lost.

14:34.088 --> 14:37.132
Which means rock is
my unlucky move.

14:37.216 --> 14:38.467
Am I wrong?

14:38.634 --> 14:43.013
It's only natural I'd be averse
to using my unlucky rock a third time.

14:43.222 --> 14:45.641
Since you said
I was on a losing streak,

14:45.766 --> 14:47.809
you won't be able to use paper.

14:47.851 --> 14:50.228
Your using paper would
be an admission

14:50.270 --> 14:52.814
that I am not in the middle
of a losing streak.

14:53.732 --> 14:55.400
You're going down!

14:57.611 --> 14:59.571
Let's go, Rohan Kishibe!

15:00.030 --> 15:01.197
It's time!

15:01.281 --> 15:01.990
Ro…

15:01.991 --> 15:02.741
…sham…

15:02.783 --> 15:03.867
…bo!

15:05.536 --> 15:08.163
<i>After all that bluffing,
he still used paper.</i>

15:08.205 --> 15:09.706
<i>His mental fortitude is remarkable.</i>

15:09.790 --> 15:11.583
<i>I can't lose!</i>

15:11.625 --> 15:14.127
<i>I'm definitely the one
with winning momentum here!</i>

15:14.503 --> 15:17.589
<i>I'll use paper four times in a row!
This game's in the bag!</i>

15:17.881 --> 15:19.215
<i>All right! Rock!</i>

15:19.299 --> 15:22.135
<i>I'll make misfortune work
in my favor!</i>

15:22.177 --> 15:24.012
One more…

15:27.433 --> 15:30.102
My knees are…

15:31.437 --> 15:34.022
<i>What? He's never moved
like that before!</i>

15:34.064 --> 15:37.025
<i>The only one Rohan hasn't
used yet is scissors…</i>

15:37.067 --> 15:40.528
<i>Crap… Going with paper
four times in a row is risky!</i>

15:42.114 --> 15:42.989
Crap!

15:43.073 --> 15:45.283
I guess rock wasn't unlucky,
after all!

15:48.203 --> 15:50.288
That bastard Rohan!

15:50.998 --> 15:53.041
Th-That's…

15:56.837 --> 15:59.047
Hey, Mister!

15:59.131 --> 16:02.759
Hey, Rohan-sensei. Those two are
probably Stand users, too, right?

16:03.761 --> 16:06.221
They are, right? I can feel it.

16:06.346 --> 16:07.889
Let's see how lucky I really am.

16:07.973 --> 16:11.226
If my luck has run out,
those two will come over here.

16:11.351 --> 16:13.603
If luck is on my side,

16:13.687 --> 16:15.563
they'll never dream of
coming over here.

16:15.647 --> 16:17.565
Hey, look, it's Rohan.

16:17.608 --> 16:20.402
- Hey! Hey!
- I really can't stand that guy.

16:20.486 --> 16:22.571
Let's put on a smile and
mind our own business.

16:22.613 --> 16:27.075
Hmm… Well, hmm…

16:24.239 --> 16:27.659
MENACING

16:28.660 --> 16:30.578
That child…

16:30.537 --> 16:34.582
MENACING

16:31.163 --> 16:33.206
I would guess he's likely…

16:34.708 --> 16:36.793
just another fan.

16:36.877 --> 16:38.920
See you later.

16:38.962 --> 16:40.338
See ya.

16:42.966 --> 16:47.466
It looks like luck is totally
on my side, Rohan-sensei.

16:48.931 --> 16:51.850
I've never felt more
confident about winning in my life.

16:51.892 --> 16:53.894
I've got luck protecting me!

16:53.936 --> 16:57.314
I feel like I could
survive Russian roulette

16:57.397 --> 17:00.547
With five out of six bullets
in the chamber!

16:59.775 --> 17:00.525
CRASH

17:02.277 --> 17:05.280
Even a shower of glass!

17:18.127 --> 17:22.627
Now, for the final match.
Who's gonna win, Rohan-sensei!

17:27.636 --> 17:29.220
What are you doing?

17:29.263 --> 17:32.099
Hurry up and assume
your roshambo pose.

17:32.474 --> 17:35.059
You're the one who needs to
hurry up and get started.

17:35.102 --> 17:37.687
You're looking at my next move.

17:37.771 --> 17:39.856
You can knock off the jokes, okay.

17:39.940 --> 17:41.691
I can assure you
this isn't a joke.

17:41.775 --> 17:44.235
You said you were going
to surpass me,

17:44.361 --> 17:46.488
but since I've got
nine years on you,

17:46.572 --> 17:47.823
I'll let you in on a little secret…

17:47.865 --> 17:51.660
Beating one's opponents
isn't that difficult.

17:52.452 --> 17:55.413
The real challenge is…
Now pay attention…

17:55.455 --> 17:57.498
The real challenge is…

17:58.125 --> 18:00.085
outdoing oneself!

18:00.127 --> 18:03.046
I'm going to outdo my own luck!

18:10.596 --> 18:12.306
Let's go, Rohan!

18:12.347 --> 18:13.556
It's on!

18:13.640 --> 18:16.517
Ro-sham… bo!

18:16.727 --> 18:19.896
Yes! How's that, Rohan Kishibe?!

18:20.939 --> 18:23.608
W-What?

18:23.817 --> 18:26.236
- What?!
- Huh?

18:27.446 --> 18:29.281
W-What the—?

18:29.323 --> 18:31.867
Why am I making the rock move?!

18:34.369 --> 18:36.662
That makes three wins
and two losses.

18:36.705 --> 18:38.540
Now you've got the unlucky rock.

18:38.790 --> 18:43.290
It wasn't just Joseph Joestar
who paid me a visit. Luck did too.

18:44.630 --> 18:46.048
The Invisible Baby.

18:47.174 --> 18:48.091
Huh?!

18:48.008 --> 18:51.428
I WILL RESCUE ROHAN FROM DANGER.
I WILL TURN MYSELF INVISIBLE AND
MAKE THE KID'S HAND INTO "ROCK".

18:51.595 --> 18:54.389
You were over-reliant on luck,

18:54.431 --> 18:56.975
whereas I took it upon myself
to change my luck.

18:57.184 --> 19:00.061
That is the meaning of
outdoing oneself.

19:00.354 --> 19:02.105
BOOM

19:04.191 --> 19:06.026
Now, then, as I promised,

19:06.068 --> 19:08.779
I shall now render you
out of commission.

19:09.279 --> 19:10.405
For I'll write,

19:10.614 --> 19:14.451
"I shall never again win
another game of roshambo.

19:14.534 --> 19:16.744
My Stand shall
be reduced to tatters."

19:16.828 --> 19:19.413
Sh-Shut up!

19:19.665 --> 19:22.542
Stay away from me, Rohan!

19:23.543 --> 19:26.254
O-Otherwise, this baby's gonna…

19:27.381 --> 19:30.592
Do you understand
what you're doing?

19:30.634 --> 19:33.386
Hmph! We've moved on now
to a war of words!

19:33.428 --> 19:35.388
You didn't really beat me!

19:35.472 --> 19:38.099
You did nothing
but cheat, you coward!

19:38.183 --> 19:40.476
Surrender the baby, now.

19:40.602 --> 19:42.312
Battle me one more time!

19:42.437 --> 19:44.897
Do that and the baby
remains safe and sound.

19:45.065 --> 19:48.401
What about "surrender the baby"
do you not understand…

19:49.528 --> 19:50.862
I'll humor you.

19:59.746 --> 20:04.246
Get ready to lose!
Ro-sham! Bo! Bo!

20:07.212 --> 20:10.089
I-I-I can't win!

20:13.302 --> 20:16.221
Blast it! I went through all the trouble

20:16.263 --> 20:18.306
to turn you into a Stand user
and you blew it!

20:18.598 --> 20:20.391
Sayonara!

20:20.475 --> 20:21.976
You won't die.

20:22.060 --> 20:24.812
I'm simply going to
wipe out your Stand.

20:24.980 --> 20:26.106
If…

20:26.398 --> 20:29.984
If I have to live life
under the shadow of your writing…

20:30.694 --> 20:34.948
If I have to live under
your psychological control…

20:37.367 --> 20:39.243
I'd rather die under
this giant truck!

20:39.286 --> 20:41.496
Take that, Rohan Kishibe!

20:41.913 --> 20:42.914
PFFT

20:43.332 --> 20:45.876
Bravo. I like you, kid.

20:45.959 --> 20:50.254
It's people who have a flare
for comic book-like action that really…

20:50.088 --> 20:50.838
DASH

20:50.380 --> 20:50.860
pull at my heartstrings!

21:00.307 --> 21:00.849
Wha—?!

21:00.849 --> 21:02.684
Y-You'll be run over, too!

21:02.768 --> 21:03.602
You think so?

21:04.686 --> 21:06.771
What the—? Th-The wind!

21:06.813 --> 21:09.357
Whoa, what the hell
is this picture?!

21:09.399 --> 21:12.276
I-I can't see!

21:20.786 --> 21:23.079
I-It swerved at just
the last second.

21:23.914 --> 21:28.414
Y-You could have died, too,
but, for me, you…

21:28.668 --> 21:30.795
Was it luck?

21:31.546 --> 21:33.172
In a relatively short period,

21:33.215 --> 21:35.550
you've become quite
the extraordinary individual.

21:36.009 --> 21:37.802
I won't render you
out of commission.

21:38.011 --> 21:41.347
However, you must not
use your Stand for evil.

21:42.766 --> 21:46.311
Of course, I had to run into
that damn thing, damn it!

21:49.231 --> 21:52.943
I lost. I've completely lost.

21:53.318 --> 21:55.945
Hey, Rohan!

21:56.196 --> 21:59.115
D-Did you find the baby?

21:59.199 --> 22:01.326
She's missing, Sensei!

22:02.702 --> 22:05.913
N-No, she may've gone
invisible again.

22:05.956 --> 22:07.332
D-Dammit…

22:08.375 --> 22:09.376
She's gone.

22:09.418 --> 22:11.169
Hey, where are you?

22:11.211 --> 22:13.421
<i>I'll just pretend like
nothing ever happened…</i>

22:13.463 --> 22:16.674
W-Where did you go?
Where are you?

22:16.842 --> 22:17.926
<i>Rosham Boy</i>

22:18.009 --> 22:19.969
<i>- Real name: Ken Oyanagi.</i>
- Hey!

22:20.053 --> 22:22.221
<i>Stand name: Boys Man Man.</i>

22:22.264 --> 22:23.765
<i>Not out of commission.</i>

22:23.807 --> 22:26.226
<i>Though, the hole
in his cheek remains.</i>

23:38.298 --> 23:41.509
EPISODE 27
I'M AN ALIEN
